{
  "version": 1,
  "templateKind": "TEAM_PROPOSAL",
  "notes": "Hand-authored workspace-default binding for the Team Proposal v1 docx. seed: {\"name\":\"Team Proposal\",\"version\":\"v1\",\"kind\":\"TEAM_PROPOSAL\"}. Per-role iteration choice: the engine's resolveEngineField() in engine-outputs.ts only matches the regex /^([\\w]+)\\[\\*\\]\\.(.+)$/ — it supports `roles[*].field` but NOT `roles[0].field`/`roles[1].field`/etc. So this docx exposes each per-role column as a single placeholder (one row per concept, not one row per role) and the docx filler joins the array with ', '. A row-per-role layout would require a real docx engine with table-row repetition (Slice 5+). The static line «Additional roles, if any, listed in appendix.» under the team table is intentionally not bound — there is no engine field for «+N more». Cap of 5 roles called for in the brief is enforced visually in the appendix narrative, not by the binding (the comma-joined list will simply include all roles the engine surfaces).",
  "entries": [
    {
      "field": "project.name",
      "target": { "kind": "docx.placeholder", "token": "{{project_name}}" },
      "format": "auto",
      "note": "Cover > project name."
    },
    {
      "field": "engagement.clientName",
      "target": { "kind": "docx.placeholder", "token": "{{client_name}}" },
      "format": "auto",
